# ── Site ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.nextlevelgrowth.com

# ── Email delivery (Resend) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real production email for the Growth Coach's internal lead notification
# and the visitor's personalized plan email, plus the Growth Audit and
# Contact form notifications. Until RESEND_API_KEY and EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS
# are BOTH set, every route falls back to logging the email to the server
# console instead — submissions are still saved, nothing is silently lost.
#
# Setup: create a Resend account (resend.com), verify a sending domain
# under Domains (add the TXT/CNAME/MX records it gives you at your DNS
# provider), then create an API key under API Keys. See the completion
# report for the full step-by-step, including how to send a test email.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Where the internal "new lead" notification is sent.
LEAD_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL=hello@nextlevelgrowthagency.com
# Must be an address on the domain you verified in Resend (e.g. reports@yourdomain.com).
EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=

# EMAIL_FROM_NAME is prepended to the sender header (e.g. "Next Level Growth <reports@yourdomain.com>").
EMAIL_FROM_NAME=Next Level Growth
# Default reply-to for sends that don't set one explicitly (most routes
# already set replyTo to the specific visitor's address per-send; this is
# the fallback).
EMAIL_REPLY_TO=hello@nextlevelgrowthagency.com

# CRM integration (optional — no adapter is wired up yet; leave blank).
CRM_API_KEY=
CRM_ENDPOINT_URL=

# ── Durable database + Auth (Supabase) ──────────────────────────────────
# Until NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are BOTH
# set: leads/inquiries and analytics events are held in-memory only (reset
# on every server restart, never shared across serverless instances), and
# /admin/* is hard-blocked in production entirely (src/middleware.ts) —
# the public site still works end to end either way, it's only durability
# and the owner dashboard that are affected. Setup: create a project at
# supabase.com, run every file in supabase/migrations/ in numeric order
# (0001 through 0008 as of this writing) in the SQL Editor, then copy
# these three values from Project Settings → API. Once all three are set
# and deployed, the FIRST real signup creates a 'prospect' profile
# automatically (migration 0003's trigger) — promote that one account to
# owner with:
#   update profiles set role = 'owner' where email = 'you@yourdomain.com';
# run once in the Supabase SQL Editor. That account can then sign in at
# /admin/login and reach the dashboard immediately.
#
# The URL is not a secret — it's the same value used by the browser/SSR
# Supabase clients below, hence NEXT_PUBLIC_. Only the service-role key is
# a secret.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# Server-only — never exposed to the browser, bypasses Row Level Security.
# Used by src/lib/growth-coach/adapters/supabase.ts (leads/inquiries) and
# analytics-events-supabase.ts (first-party admin dashboard events).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# Safe to expose to the browser (that's the point — protected entirely by
# RLS policies, see supabase/migrations/0003). Required in addition to the
# URL above for real Signup/Login/Portal/Admin-by-role to activate; without
# it those pages render a clear "not configured" message instead of a
# broken form. See supabase/migrations/0003_profiles_and_role_based_access.sql.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Spam protection (Cloudflare Turnstile) ──────────────────────────────
# Both blank = the widget doesn't render and server-side verification is
# skipped (submissions still work — honeypot + rate limiting stay active
# either way). Setup: create a Turnstile widget at the Cloudflare
# dashboard → Turnstile, add your domain, copy the site key and secret key.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# ── Growth Coach ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAT_ENABLED gates the whole widget (leave false to hide it
# entirely). Once it's true, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY controls whether
# open-ended replies come from a real Claude model — structured turns
# (prompt cards, the Growth Score assessment, scripted flows) are always
# deterministic either way. Leave ANTHROPIC_API_KEY blank to run the
# whole coach on the scripted engine only (same behavior as before this
# was wired up); every free-text reply automatically falls back to it
# anyway if the API call fails or times out, so this is always safe to
# leave unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAT_ENABLED=false
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Defaults to claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 if unset — see
# src/lib/growth-coach/ai/config.ts for the pricing assumption behind the
# cost estimates this produces.
GROWTH_COACH_MODEL=

# ── Growth Coach AI usage limits + monthly cost circuit breaker ─────────
# Per-visitor daily message caps (open AI conversation turns only —
# scripted/structured turns are always free and uncapped). "guest" = not
# signed in, "free" = signed in without the 'client' profile role, "client"
# = signed in with role 'client'. All optional; defaults shown below.
GROWTH_COACH_GUEST_DAILY_LIMIT=8
GROWTH_COACH_FREE_DAILY_LIMIT=30
GROWTH_COACH_CLIENT_DAILY_LIMIT=50
#
# Two independent monthly cost ceilings (USD) — the global safety net on
# top of the daily caps above. AI_MONTHLY_FREE_BUDGET_USD covers all
# guest + free-account usage combined; AI_MONTHLY_CLIENT_BUDGET_USD covers
# paying-client usage separately, so one pool running out never affects
# the other. Each resets automatically at the start of the next calendar
# month (see AI_BUDGET_TIMEZONE) — no manual reset needed. Once a pool
# hits its ceiling, every visitor in it gets the scripted Growth Coach
# fallback (lead capture keeps working normally) until the reset. An
# alert email is sent to LEAD_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL at 80% and 100% of each
# pool, labeled with which pool triggered it. Cost is Stage 2's estimate
# from real token counts against a hard-coded published-pricing
# assumption (see PRICING_USD_PER_MILLION_TOKENS in
# src/lib/growth-coach/ai/config.ts) — not a billing-grade number.
AI_MONTHLY_FREE_BUDGET_USD=100
AI_MONTHLY_CLIENT_BUDGET_USD=100
# IANA timezone used to compute daily/monthly boundaries for the limits
# above (e.g. "America/Chicago", "America/Los_Angeles").
AI_BUDGET_TIMEZONE=America/New_York

# ── Analytics ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# ── Growth Coach owner dashboard (DEVELOPMENT-ONLY AUTH) ────────────────
# A single shared dev password gating /admin/* IN DEVELOPMENT ONLY — never
# store the plaintext password itself, only the hash below. Generate one
# locally (see src/lib/growth-coach/auth/session.ts) and set it in your own
# .env.local, never here or in source control. Leave blank to keep /admin
# inaccessible. IMPORTANT: regardless of these two variables, this dev
# password form is NEVER reachable in production — three independent
# checks all key off NODE_ENV === "production": src/middleware.ts hard-
# blocks every /admin/* page except /admin/login, that page itself only
# renders the password form outside production (showing a safe "not
# configured" message instead), and /api/admin/login independently
# refuses to accept a POST at all. Once Supabase Auth is configured (see
# above), production ignores this entirely and uses real sign-in instead.
GROWTH_COACH_ADMIN_DEV_PASSWORD_HASH=
GROWTH_COACH_SESSION_SECRET=
